      "generated_answer": "The Dieterici equation of state is $ P(V - nb')\\exp\\left(\\frac{na'}{RTV}\\right) = nRT $. At the critical point, the first and second derivatives of $ P $ with respect to $ V $ (at constant $ T $) vanish. For the Dieterici equation, standard derivation yields $ V_c = 2nb' $, $ T_c = \\frac{a'}{4Rb'} $, and $ P_c = \\frac{a'}{4e^2b'^2} $. Solving these gives $ b' = \\frac{V_c}{2} $ and $ a' = 2RT_cV_c $. This matches option A.\n\nA. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 2)\n\n\\boxed{A}",
