    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The quantum efficiency of 0.1 means that, on average, 10 out of 100 photons are detected. The detection process follows a binomial distribution, so the rms deviation (standard deviation) is √(n·p·(1−p)) = √(100·0.1·0.9) = √9 = 3. Thus, the correct answer is an average of 10 with an rms deviation of about 3.  \n\\boxed{B}",
