g 5 rectangular faces. Plus 2 triangular ends = 7? But that contradicts options. Re-examining: if the prisms are attached so that their rectangular faces align *perfectly*, and the rectangles are congruent, then attaching three in a row creates a solid with two triangular ends and a continuous rectangular “band” of 3 × 3 = 9 rectangles? No—each attachment merges two rectangles into one, so 9 − 2 = 7 rectangles, plus 2 triangles = 9. Yes: 3 prisms × 3 rectangles = 9 rectangles; 2 attachments merge 2 pairs → subtract 2 → 7 rectangles; 2 triangular bases remain → 7 + 2 = 9 faces. So answer is 9.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
