      "generated_answer": "We use the identity: L{f(t)/t} = ∫_s^∞ F(u) du, and recall that L{2 sinh t} = 2/(s² - 1). Differentiating the given transform: d/ds [log((s+1)/(s-1))] = d/ds [log(s+1) - log(s-1)] = 1/(s+1) - 1/(s-1) = -2/(s² - 1). Since L{t f(t)} = -F'(s), we have L{t f(t)} = 2/(s² - 1) = L{2 sinh t}, so t f(t) = 2 sinh t ⇒ f(t) = 2 sinh t / t.  \nThus, the correct answer is option D.  \n\n\\boxed{D}",
