    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output SNR for an FM receiver is given by the formula: $ \\text{SNR}_o = (3\\beta^2) \\cdot \\text{SNR}_i $, where $ \\text{SNR}_i = 40 \\, \\text{dB} $. Converting to linear scale: $ \\text{SNR}_i = 10^4 $, then computing $ \\text{SNR}_o $ for $ \\beta = 5, 10, 105 $ yields approximately 750,000; 30,000,000; and 33,075,000,000, which convert back to ~58.7 dB, ~64.7 dB, and ~85.185 dB. Thus, the correct answer is **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
