    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10292",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A long cylindrical log of specific gravity (2/3) will float in water with its axis horizontal. As its length gradually is reduced it will float in the same position. If its length is reduced so that it is only a fraction of its diameter, it will float with its axis vertical. What is its diairieter-to-length ratio for which it will just float with its axis vertical?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.5\nB. 2.5\nC. 1.33\nD. 0.8\nE. 2.0\nF. 0.5\nG. 1.1\nH. 1.75\nI. 1.0\nJ. 1.25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For a floating cylinder of specific gravity $ \\sigma = \\frac{2}{3} $, the fraction submerged when horizontal is $ \\sigma $, so the submerged depth is $ \\frac{2}{3}D $ (where $ D $ is diameter). For vertical orientation to be just stable (i.e., neutral equilibrium), the metacentric height $ GM = 0 $. Using the formula $ GM = \\frac{I}{V} - \\frac{V_{sub}}{A} $, where $ I = \\frac{\\pi D^4}{64} $, $ V = \\frac{\\pi D^2 L}{4} $, and $ V_{sub} = \\sigma V $, setting $ GM = 0 $ yields $ \\frac{D^2}{16L} = \\sigma $, so $ \\frac{D}{L} = \\sqrt{16\\sigma} = \\sqrt{16 \\cdot \\frac{2}{3}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{32}{3}} \\approx \\sqrt{10.666} \\approx 3.266 $? Wait—this is incorrect. Actually, for vertical floating, the condition for neutral stability (just vertical) is when the center of buoyancy and center of gravity align such that the metacentric height is zero. For a cylinder of length $ L $, diameter $ D $, specific gravity $ \\sigma $, the submerged length is $ \\sigma L $. The metacentric radius $ BM = \\frac{I}{V_{sub}} = \\frac{\\pi D^4 / 64}{\\pi D^2 (\\sigma L)/4} = \\frac{D^2}{16 \\sigma L} $. The distance $ BG = \\frac{L}{2} - \\frac{\\sigma L}{2} = \\frac{L(1 - \\sigma)}{2} $. Setting $ GM = BM - BG = 0 $ gives $ \\frac{D^2}{16 \\sigma L} = \\frac{L(1 - \\sigma)}{2} $, so $ \\frac{D^2}{L^2} = 8 \\sigma (1 - \\sigma) $. With $ \\sigma = \\frac{2}{3} $, $ \\sigma(1 - \\sigma) = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{2}{9} $, so $ \\frac{D^2}{L^2} = 8 \\cdot \\frac{2}{9} = \\frac{16}{9} $, hence $ \\frac{D}{L} = \\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.333 $. This matches option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 242,
        "output_tokens": 595,
        "total_tokens": 837
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
