      "generated_answer": "The given equation is a linear state-space system with impulse input $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $, and the solution is $ X(t) = e^{At}X_0 + \\int_0^t e^{A(t-\\tau)}b\\delta(\\tau)d\\tau $. The impulse response term evaluates to $ e^{A \\cdot 0}b = b $, so the total solution at $ t=0^+ $ is $ X(0^+) = X_0 + b $. Given $ X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ -22 \\end{bmatrix} $ and $ b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, we get $ X(0^+) = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ -20 \\end{bmatrix} $. The question likely asks for the first component, which is 0.\n\n$\\boxed{C}$",
