    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the open-circuit EMF, use the formula: $ E = 4.44 \\cdot f \\cdot \\phi \\cdot N \\cdot K_p \\cdot K_d $, where $ f = 60 $ Hz, $ \\phi = 0.025 $ Wb, $ N = 6 \\text{ poles} \\times 12 \\text{ slots/pole} \\times 4 \\text{ conductors/slot} / 2 = 144 $ turns (since 2 conductors = 1 turn), $ K_p = \\sin(150^\\circ/2) = \\sin(75^\\circ) \\approx 0.966 $ (five-sixths pitch), and $ K_d = \\sin(30^\\circ / 2) / \\sin(30^\\circ / 2) = 1 $ for single-layer full-pitch (but here distributed, actual $ K_d \\approx 0.956 $). Calculating: $ E \\approx 4.44 \\times 60 \\times 0.025 \\times 144 \\times 0.966 \\times 0.956 \\approx 425 $ V.  \nThe correct answer is $\\boxed{\\text{C}}$.",
