    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The safety evaluation of a food substance relies on toxicity and dose-response data from animal studies, along with human exposure data to estimate real-world risk. Among the options, the daily intake of the substance by humans consuming the food (Option G) is critical for establishing the margin of exposure and comparing it to the no-observed-adverse-effect level (NOAEL) from animal studies. While other options (e.g., lifetime intake, excretion, natural presence) may provide supplementary context, daily human intake is the standard metric used in regulatory assessments like Acceptable Daily Intake (ADI) derivations.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
