    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, insulin deficiency leads to increased activity of hormone-sensitive lipase in adipose tissue, promoting lipolysis and releasing free fatty acids into the bloodstream. These free fatty acids are taken up by the liver and esterified into triglycerides, which are then packaged into VLDL for secretion, resulting in elevated triglyceride and VLDL levels. Additionally, insulin deficiency reduces activation of lipoprotein lipase (which requires insulin), impairing triglyceride clearance from plasma.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
