      "generated_answer": "Diane will know the hit man has killed Camilla when she finds the blue key, as he explicitly tells her that the key will be her indicator once the job is done. The blue key symbolizes the completion of the murder, tying back to the earlier mystery in the film’s illusionary narrative. When she later locates the key, it confirms Camilla’s death—and triggers her psychological collapse.  \n\\boxed{\\text{She will know when she finds the blue key.}}",
