      "generated_answer": "The phrase \"In pace requiescat\" is Latin for \"May he rest in peace.\" It is often used as a solemn expression wishing peace to the dead. In the context of *The Cask of Amontillado*, it is used ironically by the narrator after entombing Fortunato alive.\n\n\\boxed{May he rest in peace}",
