    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Norman's socialist commune on Ventura Island failed because the workers, knowing they were guaranteed nine hours of pay regardless of output, deliberately slowed their work, leading to plummeting productivity. Additionally, the leadership under the Wolves was authoritarian and inept—Herman Wolf stole Norman’s gold-finding device, and Catherine Wolf abandoned the commune, deeming it too capitalistic. Ultimately, Norman’s idealism was undermined by human nature and lack of effective governance, requiring external intervention by his father and the Governor to restore order and replace the Red Flag with the American one.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{Norman's socialist commune failed due to worker laziness from guaranteed pay, authoritarian mismanagement by the Wolves, and lack of effective governance, necessitating state intervention to restore order.}}",
