    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Benedict Arnold's death instead of wounding at the Battle of Quebec in 1775 led to a British victory at the Battles of Saratoga in 1777, which prevented American colonial success and caused the American Revolution to fail. This pivotal change also stifled the French Revolution and prevented the Napoleonic Wars, altering the entire geopolitical landscape of Europe and the Americas. As a result, Britain retained control over its North American colonies and historical figures like Wellington never rose to prominence in the same way. \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Benedict Arnold's death led to a British victory at Saratoga, causing the American Revolution to fail and preventing the Napoleonic Wars.}}",
