    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Trevor and Ellen didn’t have a romantic relationship because Garfield’s destabilizing behavior and violent actions alienated Ellen, who ultimately disavowed his methods. Though they developed a close friendship, Ellen could not reconcile her moral boundaries with his escalating brutality. Her departure from the school after learning he killed Benny and mutilated César sealed the end of any romantic possibility.  \n\n\\boxed{{Ellen disavowed Garfield's violent actions, preventing any romantic relationship from developing.}}",
