      "generated_answer": "The subsistence practices of past peoples—such as diet, hunting, and gathering—are most directly inferred from the remains of animals they consumed, i.e., the faunal assemblage. While other options may provide contextual information, only the faunal assemblage offers direct evidence of what people ate and how they obtained food. Thus, the best answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
