r feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The speaker in the second passage laments that despite national independence, social conditions—especially for women and the poor—remained unchanged, indicating that liberation from colonial rule did not translate into social or economic reform. The most likely factor preventing progress is the prioritization of national liberation over social reform, as new regimes often focused on political sovereignty rather than addressing gender inequality or poverty. This aligns with historical patterns in post-colonial states, where liberation movements deferred internal social change.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
