      "generated_answer": "The most important factor in the defeats of Democratic presidential candidates in 1952 and 1968 was the Democratic Party's perceived weakness on national security issues, especially amid Cold War anxieties and growing public disillusionment with the Vietnam War, as reflected in Kerry’s testimony. While civil rights and other issues played roles, national security concerns dominated voter sentiment during these election cycles.  \n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
