      "generated_answer": "The Counterculture Movement of the 1960s was most directly galvanized by opposition to U.S. involvement in Vietnam and the draft, which sparked widespread protests and civil disobedience. While civil rights and other issues were important, the anti-war sentiment and resistance to conscription were central unifying themes. Thus, the best answer is H: U.S. involvement in Vietnam and the civil rights movement, as both were foundational to the movement’s activism.  \n\\boxed{H}",
