    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Brown v. Board of Education decision addressed racial segregation in schools, a legacy of unfulfilled promises of equality after the Civil War. Reconstruction (1865–1877) aimed to secure civil rights for formerly enslaved people, including access to education, but those promises were largely abandoned after its end. Thus, desegregation was a response to Reconstruction’s unfulfilled guarantees.  \n\\boxed{D}",
