      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **D. Reconstruction**, because the Fourteenth Amendment’s Equal Protection Clause—cited in *Brown v. Board of Education*—was enacted during Reconstruction to guarantee civil rights for formerly enslaved people, yet segregation persisted despite this promise. *Brown* directly challenged the system of racial segregation that undermined Reconstruction-era constitutional guarantees. While other initiatives like the Civil Rights Act (J) came later, Reconstruction was the foundational period whose promises remained unfulfilled, leading to the *Brown* decision.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
