      "generated_answer": "Voltaire’s satire in *Candide* targets blind optimism and dogmatic rationalism, especially Leibniz’s claim that this is the “best of all possible worlds,” a view most directly challenged by David Hume’s empirical skepticism and critique of metaphysical optimism. Hume, like Voltaire, questioned abstract rational systems that ignored human suffering and empirical reality. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.",
