    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Pangloss’s unwavering belief that “everything happens for the best,” despite overwhelming suffering, mirrors the Enlightenment optimism that the universe operates according to rational, harmonious laws—here, Leibniz’s “pre-established harmony.” This aligns with option J, which reflects the deterministic, orderly view of the universe held by some Enlightenment thinkers. Voltaire uses this to satirize blind faith in rationalism, not endorse it.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
