      "generated_answer": "The question asks for the change **least beneficial to the defense of France** during the radical phase (c. 1793–1794), when Robespierre led the Committee of Public Safety. While many measures like conscription (J), the Reign of Terror (B), price controls (E), and rationing (H) directly supported war mobilization and internal stability, **the new Republican Calendar (I)** was primarily symbolic and ideological—with no military or logistical utility for defense. Though de-Christianization (D) and expelling foreign diplomats (C) had some political utility, the Republican Calendar was largely irrelevant to practical defense efforts.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
